# Normalise to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Authoring happens on Windows; anything that runs does so on Linux (the HA OS
# VM, the forge's runners). A CRLF checkout of a shell script or a YAML document
# is a different file to every consumer that matters, and the difference is
# invisible in an editor.
#
# Today the blobs are already clean - `git cat-file blob` reports zero CR bytes
# across every tracked file - because core.autocrlf is set on this clone. That
# is a local setting on one machine, which is exactly why it should not be what
# the repository depends on.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.proto text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.apk binary
